    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a053861f_a8a1bc51",
        "filename": "avmd/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-19T15:06:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s (\u003cindex\u003e, \u003cnamespace\u003e, ...) isn\u0027t it?\nI\u0027m not sure what the indexes are though. Could you generate them using Iterator::enumerate?\n\nCould you replace NamespaceNameFileIterator with itertools::tuples() ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 32,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "492ad6a05be1d5e8443ce91c2b7f95677e013f4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "00cba605_f8183a5f",
        "filename": "avmd/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-20T11:40:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Could you generate them using Iterator::enumerate?\n\nThe indices here are the global indices of the matched arguments[1]. They are not equal to the local enumerate indices of this group. We need the global indices to preserve the original order for the output.\n\n\u003e Could you replace NamespaceNameFileIterator with itertools::tuples()?\nI don\u0027t think we can use itertools::tuples() directly here as `values` is not a continuous array. Each item in `values` corresponds to the first parameter in the triplet (\u003cnamespace\u003e, \u003cname\u003e, \u003cfile\u003e).\n\nIn fact, we could avoid all this complexity here if clap::ArgMatches could provide some simple iter method as suggested in [2], but it looks like this is not available yet.\nAnother option is to use `std::env::args` directly, since we only want to read the args in order with a fixed window. But that\u0027s hard to extend for more use cases later and we also lose other support of clap.\n\nDo you know a simpler way to do this?\n\n[1] https://docs.rs/clap/latest/clap/parser/struct.ArgMatches.html#method.indices_of \n[2] https://github.com/clap-rs/clap/issues/1206",
      "parentUuid": "a053861f_a8a1bc51",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 32,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "492ad6a05be1d5e8443ce91c2b7f95677e013f4f",
